					<category term="PyBullet Support and Feedback" scheme="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewforum.php?f=24" label="PyBullet Support and Feedback"/>
		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=44515#p44515"><![CDATA[
PyBullet’s `createCollisionShape` doesn’t directly support half cylinders, but you can create one by modeling it as a mesh in a tool like Blender,<a href="https://block-blast.io" class="postlink"><span style="color:#FFFFFF"><span style="font-size:1%;line-height:116%">Block Blast</span></span></a> exporting it as an `.obj` file, and loading it with `GEOM_MESH` in PyBullet.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=14532">otis</a> — Thu Mar 06, 2025 6:16 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
